  "unreadable": [],
  "notes": "Both images show the same pinout; transcribed separately per rule 11. Label = printed GPIO name; silkscreen spelling (TXO, RXI, 3V) first in functions, then the CircuitPython name and outward. Green 'Power Domain' tags (RTC, CPU, SPI/CPU) omitted as category-only tags. Underscores in ADCx_CHy rendered faintly. BOOT and DEBUG pads have only silkscreen labels. RESET/BOOT/DOWN/UP buttons, NeoPixel, LED, BOOT0, accelerometer interrupt, 5V/3V indicator LEDs and 3V/5V and 8/16 solder jumpers are not wiring points and were skipped. HUB75 position 1 choice is ambiguous: the detached drawing has no board edge, so the outer/inner row rule could not be applied; the key notch on the drawing's left side could alternatively imply the right column is the outer row."
}